The NCR 53C710 Zorro III SCSI-2 boards -- Commodore A4091, A4092 and A4770 --
as controllers of AMIX's SCSI disk layer: their drives are ordinary dd disks,
/dev/dsk and /dev/rdsk cNdUsS at their SCSI IDs, so AMIX can boot with root
on an A4091.  The driver is amigaux's A4091 driver by Jussi Alanaerae (MIT),
linked into the kernel with polled I/O, as kits for the stock 68030 kernel
and the 68040/060 port kernel (there through the port's DMA cache service).
No AMIX kernel is included.
